From c7ea25480f437914a3c07572ae8c29fa1dad8607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Thomas <justmoon@members.fsf.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:44:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: Add SHAMap branches for any key and all validations
 of a ledger

`SHAMap::getProofBranch` returns the branch from the root towards a key,
each node serialized with its hash prefix, so that the hash of each node is
the SHA-512Half of its bytes. Unlike `getProofPath`, which serves the peer
protocol and fails for a key the map does not hold, it answers for any key:
the branch ends at the key's leaf, at the leaf of another key that stands
where the key would be, or at the inner node whose branch for the key is
empty. The last two prove the key absent, since a leaf sits at the
shallowest depth at which its key is unique. An empty map gives an empty
branch, as its root hashes to zero.

`Validations::getAllForLedger` returns every validation held for a ledger,
trusted or not, full or partial. Unlike the other accessors it does not
refresh the ledger's entry, so a caller can read validations but not keep
them alive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
